# SYN Flood Attack Detection

## Overview
Analyzed packet logs to identify a SYN flood denial-of-service attack targeting a network. The investigation revealed a high volume of connection requests originating from the same source within milliseconds, consistent with a SYN flood pattern, and traced the cause to a backlog of half-open TCP connections resulting from incomplete handshakes.

## Approach
1. Reviewed packet logs to identify abnormal traffic patterns and request volume.
2. Traced incomplete TCP handshakes to isolate the source of the backlog.
3. Confirmed the attack pattern and documented findings in a formal incident report.

## Skills Demonstrated
- Packet log analysis
- TCP/IP protocol analysis
- Denial-of-service (DoS) attack identification
- Incident documentation

